    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MAXO_0000092">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A medical requirement or recommendation of avoiding the consumption of large amounts of alcohol.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2019-01-19T20:54:50+00:00</dc:date>
        <rdfs:comment>A medical requirement or recommendation of avoiding the consumption of large amounts of alcohol.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Excessive alcohol avoidance</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MAXO_0000653">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Treatment with a class of agents that act by selectively inhibiting angiotensin II receptor activation in the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2020-06-04T17:31:52+00:00</dc:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CHEBI:61016</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NCIT:C66930</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>ARB therapy</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>treatment with ARB</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>treatment with angiotensin II receptor antagonist</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>treatment with angiotensin II receptor blocker</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>treatment with angiotensin receptor antagonist</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>A pharmaceutical agent that selectively inhibits angiotensin II receptor activation in the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system reducing production and secretion of aldosterone, amongst other actions. The combined effects result in reduction of blood pressure. It is primarily used for the reduction of proteinuria and the treatment of hypertension in cases where the patient is intolerant of ACE inhibitor therapy.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>Angiotensin II receptor antagonists bind to and block the activation of angiotensin II type 1 (AT1) receptors, thereby reducing production and secretion of aldosterone, amongst other actions. The combined effects result in reduction of blood pressure. Although this class of agents is also used in diabetic nephropathy (kidney damage due to diabetes) and congestive heart failure, it is primarily used for the treatment of hypertension in cases where the patient is intolerant of ACE inhibitor therapy.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Angiotensin receptor blocker therapy</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MAXO_0000653"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A pharmaceutical agent that selectively inhibits angiotensin II receptor activation in the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system reducing production and secretion of aldosterone, amongst other actions. The combined effects result in reduction of blood pressure. It is primarily used for the reduction of proteinuria and the treatment of hypertension in cases where the patient is intolerant of ACE inhibitor therapy.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NCIT:C66930</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MAXO_0000653"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Angiotensin II receptor antagonists bind to and block the activation of angiotensin II type 1 (AT1) receptors, thereby reducing production and secretion of aldosterone, amongst other actions. The combined effects result in reduction of blood pressure. Although this class of agents is also used in diabetic nephropathy (kidney damage due to diabetes) and congestive heart failure, it is primarily used for the treatment of hypertension in cases where the patient is intolerant of ACE inhibitor therapy.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NCIT:C66930</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MAXO_0000988">
        <obo:IAO_0000115>Procedure to evaluate the structure and/or function of a particular by part or system.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <dc:date rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime">2023-03-29T20:10:49+00:00</dc:date>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>diagnostic procedure by body location</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment>Procedure to evaluate the structure and/or function of a particular by part or system.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">Diagnostic procedure by site</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#AgeGroup">
        <rdfs:comment>Age group ranges were selected based on established AF clinical risk scores, namely HARMS-AF (Segan et al. (2023)), which assigns 1 point for age between 60 and 64 and 2 points for age above 64, and CH2EST (Alonso et al. (2013)), which assigns 2 points for age above 74.  

- Below 60
- 60 - 64
- 65 - 74
- Above 74</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Age group</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#AlcoholMisuse">
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Alcohol abuse</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Alcohol use disorder</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>Alcoholism</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Alcohol misuse is when you drink in a way that&apos;s harmful, or when you&apos;re dependent on alcohol.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Alcohol misuse</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.org/afmo#AlcoholMisuse"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">Alcohol misuse is when you drink in a way that&apos;s harmful, or when you&apos;re dependent on alcohol.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>The National Health Service (NHS). https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/alcohol-misuse/</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#AtrialFibrillationEpisode">
        <rdfs:comment>A period of time during which &quot;the heart&apos;s upper chambers, called the atria, beat chaotically and irregularl [...] out of sync with the lower heart chambers, called the ventricles.&quot;</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Atrial fibrillation episode</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.org/afmo#AtrialFibrillationEpisode"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>A period of time during which &quot;the heart&apos;s upper chambers, called the atria, beat chaotically and irregularl [...] out of sync with the lower heart chambers, called the ventricles.&quot;</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>Mayo Clinic, https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/atrial-fibrillation/symptoms-causes/syc-20350624, accessed 14 July 2026.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#COPDStatus">
        <rdfs:comment>COPD status in a monitored person (present or absent)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease status</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#CardiovascularDiseaseStatus">
        <rdfs:comment>Cardiovascular disease status in a monitored person (present or absent)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Cardiovascular disease status</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#DiabetesMellitusStatus">
        <rdfs:comment>Diabetes mellitus status in a monitored person (present or absent)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Diabetes mellitus status</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#HeightGroup">
        <rdfs:comment>Height is categorised into five sex-specific groups based on population percentiles ranging from Group 1 (≤155 cm) to Group 5 (&gt;163 cm) for females and from Group 1 (≤168 cm) to Group 5 (&gt;178 cm) for males.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Height group</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#HypertensionStatus">
        <rdfs:comment>Hypertension status in a monitored person (present or absent)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Hypertension status</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#KidneyDiseaseStatus">
        <rdfs:comment>Kidney disease status in a monitored person (present or absent)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Kidney disease status</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#PRIntervalVariation">
        <rdfs:comment>Determined based on a specific threshold from the PR interval standard deviation.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>PR interval variation</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#PWaveVariation">
        <rdfs:comment>Determined based on a specific threshold from the P-wave duration standard deviation.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>P-wave variation</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#ProlongedPRInterval">
        <rdfs:comment>Determined based on a specific threshold from the median PR interval.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Prolonged PR interval</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#ProlongedPWave">
        <rdfs:comment>Determined based on a specific threshold from the median P-wave duration.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Prolonged P-wave</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#ProlongedRRInterval">
        <rdfs:comment>Determined based on a specific threshold from the median RR interval.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Prolonged RR interval</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#RRIntervalVariation">
        <rdfs:comment>Determined based on a specific threshold from the RR interval standard deviation.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>RR interval variation</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#RaceOrEthnicity">
        <rdfs:comment>Although race is a social rather than biological construct, it can be an (albeit imperfect) proxy for certain genetic traits. Because European ancestry is a risk factor for AF (Marcus et al., 2010; Roselli et al., 2018), this may explain why incidence of AF is higher among White people than in other racial groups (Dewland et al., 2013; Volgman et al., 2019).</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:comment>The racial/ethnic categories proposed in the AFMO are not intended to be prescriptive or exhaustive. They can be adapted based on what is relevant for the target population.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Race or ethnicity</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Ethnicity is a term for the ethnic group to which people belong. Usually it refers to group identity based on culture, religion, traditions, and customs. In some contexts, it is a “politically correct” term equivalent to the word “race,” which may have pejorative associations.</skos:definition>
        <skos:definition>Race is a social construct used to group people. Race was constructed as a hierarchal human-grouping system, generating racial classifications to identify, distinguish and marginalize some groups across nations, regions and the world. Race divides human populations into groups often based on physical appearance, social factors and cultural backgrounds.</skos:definition>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.org/afmo#RaceOrEthnicity"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Ethnicity is a term for the ethnic group to which people belong. Usually it refers to group identity based on culture, religion, traditions, and customs. In some contexts, it is a “politically correct” term equivalent to the word “race,” which may have pejorative associations.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>Oxford Refence https://www.oxfordreference.com/display/10.1093/oi/authority.20110803095759525, accessed 09 July 2026.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.org/afmo#RaceOrEthnicity"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Race is a social construct used to group people. Race was constructed as a hierarchal human-grouping system, generating racial classifications to identify, distinguish and marginalize some groups across nations, regions and the world. Race divides human populations into groups often based on physical appearance, social factors and cultural backgrounds.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>The National Human Genome Research Institute. https://www.genome.gov/genetics-glossary/Race</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#SleepApnoeaStatus">
        <rdfs:comment>Sleep apnoea status in a monitored person (present or absent)</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Sleep apnoea status</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#SmokingStatus">
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref xml:lang="en">UMLS:C0453996</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym xml:lang="en">Tobacco smoking behaviour</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A person&apos;s cigarette (tobacco) smoking behaviour.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Smoking status</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.org/afmo#SmokingStatus"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">A person&apos;s cigarette (tobacco) smoking behaviour.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/nhis/tobacco/tobacco_recodes.htm#anchor_1557516509294 and the New Zealand Ministry of Health https://www.health.govt.nz/our-work/preventative-health-wellness/tobacco-control/tobacco-control-information-practitioners/definitions-smoking-status.

- Smoker (a.k.a current smoker): a person who has smoked more than 100 cigarettes (including hand rolled cigarettes, cigars, cigarillos etc) in their lifetime and has smoked in the last 28 days. Includes daily and non-daily/social smokers.
- Non-smoker: composed of two groups: former smoker and never smoker.
   - Former smoker: a person who has smoked more than 100 cigarettes in their lifetime but has not smoked in the last 28 days. The international convention is to treat someone as an ex-smoker once they have been smokefree for one month (at least 28 days).
   - Never smoker: a person who has not smoked more than 100 cigarettes in their lifetime and does not currently smoke.

Dagfinn et al. (2018) noted that there is reduced risk of AF among former smokers compared to current smokers, but further research is needed to determine if the risk at some point reaches that of never smokers.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
    </owl:Axiom>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator">
        <rdfs:comment>An entity primarily responsible for making the resource.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>creator</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title">
        <rdfs:comment>A name given to the resource.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>title</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator">
        <vann:example>
        :my-report a fabio:Report ;
            dcterms:creator :john-doe .
    </vann:example>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">An entity primarily responsible for making the resource.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.org/dc/terms"/>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">has creator</rdfs:label>
        <ns:term_status xml:lang="en">stable</ns:term_status>
        <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Examples of a Creator include a person, an organization, or a service. Typically, the name of a Creator should be used to indicate the entity.</skos:scopeNote>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/license">
        <rdfs:comment>A legal document giving official permission to do something with the resource.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>license</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/phmo#AnthropometricFactor">
        <rdfs:comment>A class to group risk factors for atrial fribrillation related to a person&apos;s body, e.g. height and BMI.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Anthropometric factor</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/phmo#BMICategory">
        <rdfs:comment>For adults, BMI falls into the following categories:

- Underweight: below 18.5
- Normal: 18.5 - 24.9
- Overweight: 25.0 - 29.9
- Obese I: 30.0 - 34.9
- Obese II: 35.0 - 39.9
- Obese III: above 40.0</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>BMI category</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/phmo#DemographicFactor">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class to group risk factors for atrial fribrillation related to a person&apos;s demographics. Demographics: the qualities (such as age and sex) of a specific group of people.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Demographic factor</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/phmo#LifestyleFactor">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A class to group risk factors for atrial fribrillation related to a person&apos;s lifestyle and choices.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Lifestyle factor</rdfs:label>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/phmo#Sex">
        <rdfs:comment>Summary sex classification element based on one or more clinical observations such as an organ survey, hormone levels, and chromosomal analysis.</rdfs:comment>
        <rdfs:label>Sex</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>Summary sex classification element based on one or more clinical observations such as an organ survey, hormone levels, and chromosomal analysis.</skos:definition>
    </rdf:Description>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.org/phmo#Sex"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition"/>
        <owl:annotatedTarget>Summary sex classification element based on one or more clinical observations such as an organ survey, hormone levels, and chromosomal analysis.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy>McClure, Robert C., et al. &quot;Gender harmony: improved standards to support affirmative care of gender-marginalized people through inclusive gender and sex representation.&quot; Journal of the American Medical Informatics Association 29.2 (2022): 354-363. https://doi-org.ezproxy.uct.ac.za/10.1093/jamia/ocab196</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
    </owl:Axiom>
    


    <!-- 
    ///////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    //
    // General axioms
